  {
   "text": "Figure 16. (a) A flame of height H and a receiver (person) at distance d on flat ground; the published rule d = 4H (Butler and\nCohen 1998) keeps the radiant heat flux q″ reaching the receiver at or below 7 kW/m². (b) The computed safe separation\ndistance d* at 7 kW/m² in every burned cell of four reconstructed Korean fires (13,125 cells, baseline fuel; log count): 13,125\nof 13,125 lie below one 375 m grid cell; the largest over every fuel level is 323 m (Uljin 2022, high fuel). On the replay's front\nroad cells the median is 25 m (7,644 cell-hours). Model output; no measured flux. Source: research/kcf-radiation.",
